From: Korri <korri@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] backend/drm: resetting gamma on a CRTC without gamma succeeds

When a CRTC has neither a GAMMA_LUT property nor a legacy gamma table
(gamma_size 0), drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma() returned false for a reset
request (size 0). drm_atomic_connector_prepare() then failed the whole
commit without logging and without an ioctl. wlr_scene re-arms a gamma
reset whenever an output is re-enabled, so on such hardware (Allwinner
sun4i-drm, RG35XX Pro) the first enable after a power-off always failed
with "Backend commit failed", and only a second request succeeded.

A CRTC without gamma already has identity gamma; a reset is a no-op.
Setting a real LUT on such a CRTC still fails.

---
--- a/backend/drm/legacy.c
+++ b/backend/drm/legacy.c
@@ -255,7 +255,8 @@
 		// The legacy interface doesn't offer a way to reset the gamma LUT
 		size = drm_crtc_get_gamma_lut_size(drm, crtc);
 		if (size == 0) {
-			return false;
+			// The CRTC has no gamma LUT, so there is nothing to reset
+			return true;
 		}
 
 		linear_lut = malloc(3 * size * sizeof(uint16_t));
